1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,980
What if every chart was made of what it measures?

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:09,690
Copper: Chile mined more than the United States, China and Russia combined.

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:14,800
Coffee: Brazil grows more than the next four countries together.

4
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:20,390
Cotton: China grew more than Brazil and the United States combined.

5
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:28,300
Lithium: Australia, China and Chile mined nearly three-quarters of world output, not counting the U.S.

6
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,930
Each one was made with Plate.

7
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:34,646
Paste your data and pick a format and a style.

8
00:00:34,646 --> 00:00:37,880
Muse Spark turns your brief into a design spec.

9
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:46,000
Tencent's Hy Image 3.5 renders it on GMI Cloud, and Plate checks every label against the spec.

10
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:53,350
When Hy pointed a note about the whole chart at Zambia, Plate caught it, and one edit erased the line.

11
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:59,900
And when it printed 28,000 instead of 23,000, one edit fixed that too.

12
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:02,376
Material Facts.

13
00:01:02,376 --> 00:01:05,970
Every pixel by Hy Image 3.5.
